      "id": 4,
      "claim": "Adding a condiment to another person’s food without their consent violates personal autonomy and is judged as morally wrong by ordinary US standards.",
      "evidence": "US moral judgments treat tampering with someone’s food without permission as a breach of respect and consent, even when the ingredient is harmless; such acts are commonly labeled as rude or wrong (e.g., “don’t mess with my food”).",
